
What is API ?

“application programming interface - An API is a set of codes and rules
which allows two or more than two applications to communicate with each other
internally or externally
and provide a result to end users or to another API.“.

Acts as a middleman between different applications,
allowing them to interact
without needing to know how each other works internally.
=====================   REST vs SOAP  =========================

| **Web Service**                                                               | **API**                                                                                       |
| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Always needs a **network (web)** to communicate (HTTP/SOAP).                  | May or may not use a network. Can be local (e.g. Java API) or remote (REST API).              |
| It is a **type of API** designed for remote machine-to-machine communication. | General interface for any software component to interact with another, not restricted to web. |


✅ All web services are APIs because they provide an interface for communication between software components.
ex. RESTful API exposed over HTTP , SOAP web service for banking transactions
❌ Not all APIs are web services because some APIs are purely local and do not communicate over the web or network.
ex. java api, Android Activity Lifecycle API
