REST - Representational State Transfer
Architecture/design Style: Follows a client-server model using HTTP/HTTPS.
*** its not a protocol
Stateless - Each request from the client contains all the information needed
            (e.g., headers, parameters)to process it.
            The server doesn’t store session data between requests.
Data Format - Uses lightweight formats like JSON (mostly), XML, or plain text.
json - java script object notation
xml - eXtensible  mark up language
plain text - anything
>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
| Feature               | REST (Representational State Transfer)         | SOAP (Simple Object Access Protocol)          |
|-----------------------|-----------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------|
| **Type**              | Architectural style                           | Protocol                                      |
| **State Management**  | Stateless                                     | Can be stateful                               |
| **Data Format**       | JSON, XML, plain text                         | XML only                                      |
| **Protocol**          | HTTP/HTTPS (primarily)                        | HTTP, SMTP, TCP, etc.                         |
| **Performance**       | Faster (lightweight)                          | Slower (XML overhead)                         |
| **Security**          | HTTPS + OAuth/JWT                             | WS-Security (built-in)                        |
| **Error Handling**    | HTTP status codes                             | SOAP fault messages                           |
| **Caching**           | Supported                                    | Not natively supported                       |
| **Use Cases**         | Web/mobile apps, public APIs                 | Enterprise systems, banking, healthcare      |
| **Example**           | `GET /users/123` (JSON response)             | XML envelope with strict structure           |

