API Documentation
Access to db (third party app - db) | CRUD operation
Authorization overhead

A. Initial Setup Complexity
Requires:
Framework setup (e.g., RestAssured, Postman + Newman).
Mocking dependencies (e.g., WireMock for third-party APIs).
Test Data ( faker library )

B. Dynamic Data Handling
APIs often return changing data (e.g., timestamps, IDs).
Solutions:
Regex/JSONPath extraction.
Dynamic variable storage (e.g., pm.environment.set() in Postman).

C. Authentication & Security Testing
Handling:
OAuth 2.0, JWT tokens (token expiry issues).
Rate-limiting (avoiding false failures).

D. Flaky Tests
Tests fail due to:
Network issues.
Unstable test environments ( microservices response , unavailable due to deployment/changes )
Race conditions (e.g., async API calls).

E. Versioning & Backward Compatibility
Ensuring new API versions don’t break existing clients.
Testing deprecated endpoints.

F. CI/CD Integration
Automating tests in Jenkins/GitHub Actions requires:
Environment management (dev/staging/prod).
Test reporting (e.g., Allure, Extent Reports).

Rate Limiting

A restriction on how many API requests a client can make in a given time (e.g., *100 requests/hour*).
Prevents abuse, ensures fair usage, and protects servers from overload.
If the limit is exceeded, the API responds with:
http
HTTP/1.1 429 Too Many Requests
Retry-After: 3600  # Wait 1 hour

Race Condition

When concurrent requests cause unexpected behavior due to timing issues
 (e.g., two users booking the last ticket).

solution >>
Use Synchronization (When Necessary)
Problem: Tests need sequential execution for certain steps.
Solution:
Use synchronized blocks or
TestNG @BeforeClass.
